        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "692c3c5c-85f7-5362-9f0e-6798063c2b34",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Home Rule League, Irish Parliamentary Party\n- Concepts: Irish Home Rule movement, home rule, self-government\n- People: John Dunbar\n- Roles: Member of Parliament\n- Places: Ireland, United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland, New Ross\n\nFacts:\n- The Irish Home Rule movement agitated for self-government for Ireland within the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.\n- The Home Rule League was a political party active from 1873 to 1882 that campaigned for home rule for Ireland within the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.\n- The Home Rule League was also called the Home Rule Party and the Home Rule Confederation.\n- In February 1874, John Dunbar of the Home Rule League became the Member of Parliament for New Ross.\n- John Dunbar served as Member of Parliament for New Ross until his death in 1878.\n- The Irish Parliamentary Party replaced the Home Rule League.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "3e6c5021-e3a9-5cfd-a267-39c1b02a4716",
        "text": "Page: Home Rule League. Sentence: The Home Rule League (1873–1882), sometimes called the Home Rule Party or the Home Rule Confederation, was a political party which campaigned for home rule for Ireland within the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland, until it was replaced by the Irish Parliamentary Party.\nPage: Irish Home Rule movement. Sentence: The Irish Home Rule movement was a movement that agitated for self-government for Ireland within the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.\nPage: John Dunbar (MP). Sentence: John Dunbar was a Home Rule League politician who served as the Member of Parliament for New Ross from February 1874 through to his death in 1878.",
